Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='typstfirst', at=datetime(2026, 9, 25, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title="What is read is Typst, what reacts is TypeScript; typst's HTML is the one string the browser parses, through rich.ts", body='*Escaping is the DOM* (`web/src/view/dom.ts`: `createElement`/`textContent`; the build refuses markup parsed from a string) with ONE exception: *typst\'s HTML is the one string the browser parses, through one door (`web/src/rich.ts`).* WHAT IS READ IS TYPST, WHAT REACTS IS TYPESCRIPT (`docs/TYPST-FIRST-PLAN-2026-09-25.md`): bodies, a secretary\'s answers, the todo reading page with "Why this number" (`suzatary_core::reading`), the Inbox\'s decision prose and a day\'s briefing are all typst\'s HTML, compiled by `suzatary_io::render`. Bodies and answer blocks are cached content-addressed under `$XDG_CACHE_HOME`; a reading page prints the clock, so it lives in a bounded process memo and never on disk. `rich` travels beside the source, never instead, and a page never fetched reads as its plain text. Safe because every authored text compiles in the closed world, whose library has no `html` (no writer, the agent included, can write an element or attribute typst\'s own markup would not), and data is escaped by `escape_markup`; typst HTML-escapes text; *rendered means confirmed* (an untrusted record is served as source until `suzatary todo confirm`); and the tripwire (`suzatary_core::tripwire::suspicious`, the box\'s renderer\'s and, through the core\'s wasm, the door\'s for a page the tab compiles) REFUSES (never edits) a script element, an inline handler, a `javascript:`, `vbscript:` or `data:` URL (read as a browser reads it: references decoded, controls and spaces out, since typst writes a tab raw in an attribute), a base, an http-equiv, a form or a frame, on cache reads as well as compiles; and `rich.ts` keeps an href only of a scheme that navigates (`view/href.ts`). `scripts/web-static.sh` (run by `build-web.sh` and `web-test.sh`) fails if any other file assigns `innerHTML` or `rich.ts` holds other than exactly one. Mail bodies are `textContent`; a person\'s turn and a verb\'s answer go through `web/src/chat/refs.ts`; a model\'s answer goes through `rich.ts` block by block (typst\'s HTML; compiled in the same closed world, its preamble drawn with typst\'s own elements, the tripwire holds); a day\'s briefing (`GET /api/briefings/<date>`: that day\'s brief, block by block, or a saved file under `briefings/`) goes through the door the same way.', rationale='Decided 2026-09-25 (docs/TYPST-FIRST-PLAN-2026-09-25.md).', supersedes=()))